
Run from the repository root:

    pio run
    sh test/run_host_tests.sh

The host regressions require Python 3 and a C++11 compiler with AddressSanitizer
and UndefinedBehaviorSanitizer. They reuse ArduinoJson installed by PlatformIO.
No ESP32 connection or upload is required.

The checks compile the production RSS, meteo and eyes modules and the actual
setup/SNTP/OTA handler bodies against small host stubs. They cover bounded input,
deadlines, cache preservation, category changes, retry/rollover scheduling,
frame timing, streaming HTML substitution, credentials and filesystem recovery.
They do not measure real heap fragmentation, task stack margins, I2C latency,
TLS/radio behavior or OTA on hardware.

Validate OTA slot alignment, overlap, flash limits and built image capacity:

    pio run
    pio run --target buildfs
    python3 test/check_ota_layout.py
